# UST.G3CW Selected H11 Split-Place Base Action Theorem

## Status

`CLOSED_EXACT_SELECTED_H11_B89_BASE_ACTION_AND_REDUCED_KERNEL_AT_ONE_COMPLETELY_SPLIT_PRIME`

This is an exact finite-field execution theorem. It is not yet a
characteristic-zero or Archimedean certification.

## Statement

Let

```text
A(a,gamma) = A0(gamma) + a U(gamma) S(gamma)^-1 W(gamma)
```

be the selected H11 family from UST.G3CV, where `A0` is the unchanged B89
chart and `U`, `S`, and `W` have rank dimension `988`. At the completely split
prime `p=21817`, evaluate this family at all six roots

```text
gamma = 5, 1971, 6912, 10062, 10605, 14055.
```

For every root, the exact sparse solve

```text
A0 P = U
```

has zero residual. Six-root interpolation therefore emits the complete
`4426 x 988 x 6` power-basis residue of `P=A0^-1 U`. The theorem also emits

```text
Q = W P
```

as a `988 x 988 x 6` power-basis residue, so the selected reduced path kernel
at this prime is explicitly

```text
S + a Q.
```

## Independent Endpoint Check

At every split root, the following four independently computed determinants
are nonzero:

```text
det(A0), det(S), det(S+Q), det(A0+Delta).
```

They satisfy the fraction-free determinant-lemma identity

```text
det(A0+Delta) det(S) = det(A0) det(S+Q) mod 21817.
```

Thus all six selected endpoint specializations are invertible at this proof
prime, and the G3CV reduced kernel exactly reproduces the full corrected H11
endpoint determinant.

## What This Closes

Before this theorem, `U`, `S`, and `W` were exact but the B89 inverse had not
been applied to the selected update columns. UST.G3CW executes that action and
the complete `988`-square reduced kernel at one completely split proof prime.
It removes ambiguity about dimensions, row order, quotient elimination, and
the sign in the reduced equation.

